00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.090
from TikTok pasta to
Valentine's day candy cakes,

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.670
they're all good.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.142
Today, she's here to tell
us about her new memoir

00:00:16.142 --> 00:00:18.690
and it's called "You Were Always There,

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.600
Notes and Recipes for
Living a Life you Love",

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.130
and it's available right
now wherever books are sold.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.397
So let's welcome Danielle Kartes.

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:27.684
(Audience cheers)
(Danielle claps)

00:00:27.684 --> 00:00:29.001
Ah, here I am, here I am!
(audience applauds)

00:00:29.001 --> 00:00:30.643
This feels so good to be out here!

00:00:30.643 --> 00:00:31.480
- I know, we're in a different position -

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.030
- We're in a different position -

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.055
- We're sitting -

00:00:34.055 --> 00:00:35.480
- We're lounging -
- We're lounging-

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.070
We're in a silky dress,
- With your book.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.059
Your dress feels so soft, by the way.

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:39.892
- It's so it's silky.
- Yes.

00:00:39.892 --> 00:00:41.259
- I just wanna like roll around in it -

00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:42.567
- I know, it's kind of like,

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.439
I would sleep in that, it's so soft.

00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:45.272
- Yes.

00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:46.370
I fit feels like a little
night gowny, but great.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.241
- What did you bring though?
This is looks delicious.

00:00:48.241 --> 00:00:49.380
- Okay. This is so great.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.670
We have the brown butter,
dark chocolate bundt cake.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:53.660
- Okay.
- That's in the book.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.820
That's in the book,
"You Were Always There."

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.230
- [Kelly] It's also gonna be my mouth.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.063
- Yes, it's so delicious.

00:00:57.063 --> 00:00:58.670
And then we have the Duckhorn cab

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.420
which we can't do the
segment without some wine.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.457
- Let's pair it, yeah.

00:01:01.457 --> 00:01:02.590
- Yeah. Let's pair it, let's try.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.050
- Wait, I'm gonna, I'm gonna do the -

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.630
Wait! Wait, wait! Cheers.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.463
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

00:01:07.463 --> 00:01:08.534
- Cheers to the book,
cheers to on the couch.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.200
You know, what's so cool?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.497
So the title of the book is called.

00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:12.600
"You Were Always There."

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.750
and I feel like so often in times we feel

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.950
like we lose ourselves.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.180
I mean, to motherhood, to career change

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.080
to hard stuff that happens.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.960
And I used to think
before I wrote this book

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.602
and all the things that we,
you know, we went through

00:01:23.602 --> 00:01:25.864
I thought if I could just
get back to that girl,

00:01:25.864 --> 00:01:27.480
if I could just get back to that girl

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.630
who was a little bit thinner,

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.275
the girl that was a little
that had a different plan.

00:01:30.275 --> 00:01:33.560
No. And we, we miss out on so much life.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.790
And when I was writing this
book, I thought, you know what?

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:36.860
You were always there.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.693
You're always there.

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:38.809
That girl, that other girl she's gone,

00:01:38.809 --> 00:01:40.430
this is who we are now.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.816
And if we can embrace it and love it.

00:01:41.816 --> 00:01:43.840
So that's just been a
special thing for me.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.560
Like you get rid of the
notion that you lost yourself

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.980
because you didn't you're right here.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.770
Right where you're supposed to be and joy

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.180
and sorrow can live together.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.013
- Yeah.

00:01:52.013 --> 00:01:53.270
- And the whole idea is
I wanted people to relate

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.312
back to it.
- Yeah.

00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:56.510
- And there's just so much fun stuff.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.960
I know there's a picture
of me and Martha Stewart.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:00.040
There's a something -

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:00.873
- Oh my God.

00:02:00.873 --> 00:02:02.030
So I want you to tell this story.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:02.950
I love this story.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.080
- This is the greatest story.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.240
I feel like everybody can relate to this.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.600
I was working on a job and
there was nowhere for me to stay

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.433
at Sundance.

00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:09.266
And so I'm with this big
corporation and they're like,

00:02:09.266 --> 00:02:11.517
"Well, you can stay with our
like high level executives."

00:02:11.517 --> 00:02:12.780
I felt like an idiot.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.746
I'm like "Me, with them?"

00:02:13.746 --> 00:02:14.800
Like, I don't belong there.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:15.830
That's not for me.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:16.980
So there's nowhere for me to go.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.127
I go to this house and they're like,

00:02:18.127 --> 00:02:20.064
"Well we have this dinner
with Martha Stewart later."

00:02:20.064 --> 00:02:21.485
And I was like, "well, can I go?"

00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:23.770
And they said, "No, you can't go!

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.050
Like, you're just in the house

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.043
'cause you have to be
in the house." And...

00:02:26.043 --> 00:02:28.622
- I love that you asked
though, you never know.

00:02:28.622 --> 00:02:29.860
- Yeah, you have to ask!
- Yeah.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.000
- So then a couple minutes
later, one of the ladies knocks

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.027
on my door and she's like,

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:34.640
"You know what we were thinking about it,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.400
we're paying for it, why can't you go?"

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.320
And I was like, "Yes!"

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.220
So I get there.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.920
I didn't bring anything cute to wear.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.099
I had this weird tight blazer.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:43.807
So I throw the tight
blazer on and I'm like

00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:45.480
"I'm going to the dinner,
I'm going to the dinner."

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.130
Well, if there's only a
hundred people in this room

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.040
so I'm like trying to find her,
trying to like sneak attack

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.120
with pictures cos I'm the
weird one at the table.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.697
Have nothing in common
with any of these ladies.

00:02:52.697 --> 00:02:56.110
And I'm getting the
picture like queued up,

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.090
her she is.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.250
And we make, we literally
lock eyes in my camera

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.420
and I was like, "holy, oh
my God, please Lord kill me.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.253
I mean, don't kill me

00:03:03.253 --> 00:03:05.150
make me pass out or something."

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.120
She saw me.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.447
Then she starts walking
towards me and I'm like

00:03:07.447 --> 00:03:10.000
"I have just humiliated
myself beyond belief."

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.230
And she walks in, she walks in.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.100
I'm like "What's happening?"

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.383
And she goes, "Did we get it?"

00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:16.786
(audience laughing)

00:03:16.786 --> 00:03:18.900
- She does does have that low voice.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.917
That low voice like soothing, yeah.

00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:22.190
- And I said, "No, we didn't get it."

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.840
She goes, "Pull your phone back out."

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.187
So I pulled it out and
snapped this picture

00:03:25.187 --> 00:03:28.500
and it just, this, it was this
big light bulb moment for me.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.330
Like you belong at the
table, ask for a seat.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.680
- Yeah.
- You belong there.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.170
So this whole book is really
about really hard times living

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.960
with really great times,
being super broken, poor

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.220
and finding our way and figuring
out that you never left.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.580
- Do you think that
that drives you though?

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.220
Because I feel like that's what drove me.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.550
I had nothing to lose cuz
I had already lost so much.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.390
- And it's neat when we
share, because when you

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:51.110
share your story and your
hardship and the things

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:51.943
that you've gone through

00:03:51.943 --> 00:03:53.700
you unlock possibilities for other people.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.377
- Because they go, "Wait,
if they did it, then I can."

00:03:55.377 --> 00:03:56.210
- Then I can do it.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.690
- And when you tell somebody else,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.770
then the shame leaves too.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.720
Like, oh my gosh, I know
what that's like to wake

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.110
up in the morning and play beat the bank

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.544
hit the ATM before the red,

00:04:03.544 --> 00:04:05.724
all the bills come out
and it's red for the week.

00:04:05.724 --> 00:04:06.557
- Yeah.

00:04:06.557 --> 00:04:08.160
I think we're from the
same kind of background.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.529
- Girl. I know. We both go through forty.

00:04:10.529 --> 00:04:12.273
- Forties are gonna be so good.

00:04:12.273 --> 00:04:13.540
- [Danielle] They're so good.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:14.540
- Thank you so much, Danielle.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.373
- I love this.
- You're welcome.

00:04:15.373 --> 00:04:16.206
- We have to cook more

00:04:16.206 --> 00:04:17.180
but also do this more-
- Yes!

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.680
- And that cake is delicious.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:19.513
- Oh, it's so good here.

00:04:19.513 --> 00:04:20.695
- I just totally did.

00:04:20.695 --> 00:04:22.410
- The top is actually the best part.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.935
- I know cuz it's like kind of crispy.

00:04:23.935 --> 00:04:25.580
We are soulmates.
- So good.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.020
- Okay. Yeah. That's so good.

